+/// A follow-up's or a question's stage carries an id of its own, which may
+/// hold anything, `-end-` and `-ask-` too. A message id is a uuid, which
+/// can't (they aren't hex): the split that leaves one before the stage is
+/// the key's. A message id that isn't one (an older client's, a test's) may
+/// hold them as well, and then the stage is matched from the right, in its
+/// shortest form; a stage id holding them too can't be told apart.
 pub(crate) fn report_key_parts(key: &str, child: &str) -> Option<(String, String)> {
     let rest = key.strip_prefix("report-")?.strip_prefix(child)?.strip_prefix('-')?;
-    // A follow-up's or a question's stage carries an id of its own: the
